{
  "about": "Bar geometry in Tile-local pixels, shared by Firmware and preview. For Tiles at least 2*pad + glyph_size wide and 2*pad + max(glyph_size, track_h) high: the glyph starts at (pad,pad); the track spans the padded width, track_h tall, pad above the bottom. Capture widens the track by capture_expand_y above/below and clips to the padded Tile. Rects include their top/left and exclude bottom/right edges. The mute zone exists only when muted is declared and wins if it overlaps capture on a short Tile. Hit zone value captures only with input true; mute is a normal tap, independent of input. Unset, stale or offline values disable both zones (fresh false). Smaller Tiles have no interactive zones. A track tap alone sends nothing; a captured drag must pass ui_geo()->slop. These are contract dimensions for steps H/I, not new renderer behavior in step A.",
  "constants": {
    "pad": 20,
    "glyph_size": 32,
    "track_h": 28,
    "capture_expand_y": 24
  },
